  "promotion": "Each promoted file was rewritten with starter names and structure from the staging copy (never copied whole); \"target\" is the repo file it became, \"stagedTarget\" the path in the staging folder, so the repo file hash differs from stagedSha256. Left behind on purpose: the whole Nafath sign-in (nafath.service was hard-denied and never staged; its login tab, status polling and i18n texts were dropped on rewrite), the SSO-required 404 branch, the logout handle and form-post logout-hint delivery, the legacy id_token storage purge, the 503 exchange-deferred retry, root-redirect and the source product's BRD message catalogue codes. The rewrite follows the phase 3 contract instead: GET api/auth/modes chooser (basic, AD, SSO), #ticket/#error callback fragment cleared with history.replaceState, POST api/auth/sso/logout answering endSessionUrl for a top-level GET, activation page, and the live permission sync (focus, visibility, NavigationEnd, configurable interval) writing the signal store only on change.",
